(For completeness, the related list endpoint is `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.GET.yml`, a single `ListOwners` step under `readonly-transaction`.)

## 2. Java function classes referenced by the pipeline

All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`. Contents are given in pipeline order.

**NormalizeOwnerAddress.java** — binds `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (the only `@RequestBody` in the pipeline), normalizes address, republishes body as `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>`:
```java
public class NormalizeOwnerAddress {
    public void service(@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> body) {
        request.setAddress(OwnerAddresses.normalize(request.getAddress()));
        body.set(request);
    }
}
```

**RequireOwnerFields.java** — rejects blank firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone, throws `MissingOwnerFieldsException`:
```java
public class RequireOwnerFields {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request) throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
        List<String> missing = new ArrayList<>();
        if (isBlank(request.getFirstName())) { missing.add("firstName"); }
        if (isBlank(request.getLastName())) { missing.add("lastName"); }
        if (isBlank(request.getAddress())) { missing.add("address"); }
        if (isBlank(request.getCity())) { missing.add("city"); }
        if (isBlank(request.getTelephone())) { missing.add("telephone"); }
        if (!missing.isEmpty()) { throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing); }
    }
    private static boolean isBlank(String value) { return value == null || value.isBlank(); }
}
```

**NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java** — canonicalizes to E.164 via `OwnerTelephones.toE164`, throws `InvalidTelephoneException` on failure:
```java
public class NormalizeOwnerTelephone {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request) throws InvalidTelephoneException {
        String telephone = request.getTelephone();
        String e164 = OwnerTelephones.toE164(telephone);
        if (e164 == null) { throw new InvalidTelephoneException(telephone); }
        request.setTelephone(e164);
    }
}
```

**NormalizeOwnerEmail.java** — optional email; if present, validates and lower-cases, throws `InvalidEmailException`:
```java
public class NormalizeOwnerEmail {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request) throws InvalidEmailException {
        String email = request.getEmail();
        if (email == null || email.isBlank()) { return; }
        String normalized = OwnerEmails.normalize(email);
        if (!OwnerEmails.isValid(normalized)) { throw new InvalidEmailException(email); }
        request.setEmail(normalized);
    }
}
```

**RequireUniqueTelephone.java** — scans `ownerRepository.findAll()`, throws `DuplicateTelephoneException` on E.164 collision:
```java
public class RequireUniqueTelephone {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
            throws DuplicateTelephoneException {
        String telephone = request.getTelephone();
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (telephone.equals(OwnerTelephones.toE164(existing.getTelephone()))) {
                throw new DuplicateTelephoneException(request.getTelephone());
            }
        }
    }
}
```

**RequireUniqueHousehold.java** — rejects same-household (last name + address) unless `sharesHousehold` true; throws `DuplicateHouseholdException`:
```java
public class RequireUniqueHousehold {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
            throws DuplicateHouseholdException {
        if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) { return; }
        String key = OwnerHouseholds.key(request.getLastName(), request.getAddress());
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (key.equals(OwnerHouseholds.key(existing.getLastName(), existing.getAddress()))) {
                throw new DuplicateHouseholdException(request.getLastName(), request.getAddress());
            }
        }
    }
}
```

**RequireCityCapacity.java** — rejects when a city already has 50 owners; throws `CityAtCapacityException`:
```java
public class RequireCityCapacity {
    static final int CAPACITY = 50;
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
            throws CityAtCapacityException {
        String city = request.getCity();
        long inCity = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
            .map(Owner::getCity)
            .filter(existing -> existing != null && existing.equals(city))
            .count();
        if (inCity >= CAPACITY) { throw new CityAtCapacityException(city, CAPACITY); }
    }
}
```

**BuildOwner.java** — maps DTO to entity via `OwnerMapper.toOwner`, publishes `Out<Owner>`:
```java
public class BuildOwner {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
        built.set(ownerMapper.toOwner(request));
    }
}
```

**AssignOwnerHousehold.java** — when `sharesHousehold` true, assigns a stable `householdId` to the new and existing household members:
```java
public class AssignOwnerHousehold {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, @Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) { return; }
        String key = OwnerHouseholds.key(owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress());
        String householdId = OwnerHouseholds.id(owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress());
        owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (key.equals(OwnerHouseholds.key(existing.getLastName(), existing.getAddress()))) {
                existing.setHouseholdId(householdId);
                ownerRepository.save(existing);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

**ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate.java** — sets/normalizes the registration date (defaults to `LocalDate.now()`, rolls weekends forward). This is the effective creation-date step:
```java
public class ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
        LocalDate effective = owner.getRegistrationDate() != null ? owner.getRegistrationDate() : LocalDate.now();
        owner.setRegistrationDate(BusinessDays.rollForward(effective));
    }
}
```

**RequireDailyRegistrationCapacity.java** — rejects when 100 owners already share the (adjusted) registration date; throws `DailyRegistrationLimitException`:
```java
public class RequireDailyRegistrationCapacity {
    static final int DAILY_LIMIT = 100;
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws DailyRegistrationLimitException {
        LocalDate registrationDate = owner.getRegistrationDate();
        long registeredThatDay = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
            .map(Owner::getRegistrationDate)
            .filter(registrationDate::equals)
            .count();
        if (registeredThatDay >= DAILY_LIMIT) { throw new DailyRegistrationLimitException(DAILY_LIMIT); }
    }
}
```

**AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java** — assigns `customerCode` = per-city sequence (count in city + 1) via `OwnerCustomerCodes.format`:
```java
public class AssignOwnerCustomerCode {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        long inCity = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
            .filter(existing -> existing.getCity() != null && existing.getCity().equals(owner.getCity()))
            .count();
        int sequence = (int) inCity + 1;
        owner.setCustomerCode(OwnerCustomerCodes.format(owner.getCity(), owner.getLastName(), sequence));
    }
}
```

**AssignOwnerNamesakeCount.java** — counts existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive), sets `namesakeCount`:
```java
public class AssignOwnerNamesakeCount {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        int count = 0;
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (sameName(existing.getFirstName(), owner.getFirstName())
                    && sameName(existing.getLastName(), owner.getLastName())) { count++; }
        }
        owner.setNamesakeCount(count);
    }
    private static boolean sameName(String a, String b) { return a == null ? b == null : a.equalsIgnoreCase(b); }
}
```

**SaveOwner.java** — persists:
```java
public class SaveOwner {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        ownerRepository.save(owner);
    }
}
```

**AuditOwnerCreated.java** — logs an AUDIT entry with id, customerCode, registrationDate:
```java
public class AuditOwnerCreated {
    private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT");
    public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
        AUDIT.info("Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}",
                owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());
    }
}
```

**RespondWithOwnerCreated.java** — maps to `OwnerDto`, responds 201 Created with Location header:
```java
public class RespondWithOwnerCreated {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper,
            ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>> response) {
        OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
        response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
    }
}
```

### Supporting helper classes used by the above (same package)

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/OwnerAddresses.java` — `normalize(...)`: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST→STREET/RD→ROAD/AVE→AVENUE; null/empty → `""`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/OwnerTelephones.java` — `toE164(...)`: strips spaces/dashes/brackets, keeps leading `+` country code, else assumes `+61` (drops leading `0`); must be `\d{8,15}` or returns null.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/OwnerEmails.java` — `normalize` (trim+lowercase) and `isValid` (regex).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/OwnerHouseholds.java` — `key(lastName,address)` and `id(...)` = `"HH-" + first 12 upper-hex of SHA-256(key)`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/OwnerCustomerCodes.java` — `format(city,lastName,seq)` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (e.g. `LON-SMI-0007`). Note: the openapi doc example describes only `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, but the code prefixes a 3-letter city segment.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/BusinessDays.java` — `rollForward(date)`: pushes Sat/Sun to next Monday (does NOT skip holidays; the test helper `toBusinessDay` does skip pinned holidays).

The `OwnerMapper` used by BuildOwner/RespondWithOwnerCreated is at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` (MapStruct `@Mapper`). It derives `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), `membershipTier` (SILVER when namesakeCount==0 and email present, else BRONZE), and `locality` (from `Locality.forCity`). `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignores `id` and `pets`.

## 3. Owner entity and date field

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`** — `@Entity @Table(name="owners")`, extends `Person`. Fields:
- `address` (`@NotEmpty`)
- `city` (`@NotEmpty`)
- `telephone` (`@NotEmpty`, `@Pattern ^\+[0-9]{8,15}$` E.164)
- `email` (`@Email`)
- **`registrationDate` — `java.time.LocalDate`, `@Column(name="registration_date")`** — this is the creation/registration timestamp field (set by `ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate`). There is no separate `createdAt`/creation-timestamp field; `registrationDate` is the only date field.
- `customerCode` (`@Column customer_code`)
- `householdId` (`@Column household_id`)
- `namesakeCount` (`Integer`, `@Column namesake_count`)
- `pets` (`Set<Pet>`, `@OneToMany`)

Inherited from `Person`: `firstName`, `lastName` (and `id` from `BaseEntity`).

## 4. OwnerRepository interface

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`** — methods:
- `Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName)`
- `Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable pageable)`
- `Owner findById(int id)`
- `void save(Owner owner)`
- `Collection<Owner> findAll()`
- `Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable pageable)`
- `void delete(Owner owner)`

All declare `throws DataAccessException`.

## 5. Owner response DTO

There is no hand-written `OwnerResponse` class. The response DTO is **`OwnerDto`** (and the request DTO is **`OwnerFieldsDto`**), both **generated at build time** by the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` (v7.23.0) from the OpenAPI spec into `target/generated-sources` (package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`). They are not present as source files.

The schema is defined in **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**:
- `OwnerFields` (lines 1991–2060): `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` (required, pattern `^[0-9]*$`), `email` (optional), `registrationDate` (`format: date`, optional, defaults to server date), `sharesHousehold` (boolean, `writeOnly`, request-only, not stored).
- `Owner` (lines 2061–2140): allOf `OwnerFields` plus read-only `id`, `displayName`, `initials`, `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, `membershipTier` (enum SILVER/BRONZE → generated as `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum`), `locality`, and `pets` (array of `Pet`).

Note: the acceptance test reads back a `bulkSignupWarning` field (see below) that is not present in the `Owner` schema in openapi.yml and is not produced by any function in the current POST pipeline — worth flagging if you are implementing that behavior.

## 6. Tests related to creating owners

Only three test files exist, all under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`:

**AcceptanceTest.java** (16 lines) — the only concrete test. Extends `AcceptanceBase`; single test `coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` that creates an owner and asserts `$.bulkSignupWarning == false`:
```java
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {
    @Test
    void coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold() throws Exception {
        int id = createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
        getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.bulkSignupWarning").value(false));
    }
}
```

**AcceptanceBase.java** (322 lines) — the black-box harness. Key points:
- `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(username="acceptance-admin", roles={"OWNER_ADMIN","VET_ADMIN","ADMIN"})`. Each test rolls back; the mock user satisfies the endpoint's `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`.
- Creates owners via `POST /api/owners` and reads back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.
- Helpers: `ownerNode()` builds a fully-unique valid owner (firstName "Test", unique last name/address/city/telephone); `createOwner`, `createOwnerOk`, `createOwnerWithKey` (sends `Idempotency-Key` header), `fillCity`, `createMany`, `getOwner`, `fetchOwner`, `deleteOwner`, `extractId` (reads `id` from body or Location header).
- Unique generators: `uniqueLastName` ("Sur…"), `uniqueFirstName` ("Fn…"), `uniqueAddress`, `uniqueCity`, `uniqueTelephone` (`04XXXXXXXX`), `uniqueEmail`.
- Pinned reference data: `CITY_REGION` (Sydney→NSW, Melbourne→VIC, Brisbane→QLD), `REGION_TIMEZONE`, `REGION_POSTCODES`, `HOLIDAYS` (2026 dates), plus `toBusinessDay` (skips weekends AND holidays), `sha256hex`/`shaHex`, and `luhn`.
- References fields not yet in the pipeline/DTO: `postcode`, `addressLine1` (structured address), `Idempotency-Key`, `bulkSignupWarning`, timezone/postcode-derived values — these look like forthcoming checkpoints.

**AuditLogCapture.java** (79 lines) — test support for capturing the `AUDIT` logger output (used to assert `AuditOwnerCreated` behavior).

No `.http`/YAML fixture tests exist for owners.

## 7. Build and test commands

- Build tool: **Maven**. `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml` present (artifactId `spring-petclinic-rest`, parent `spring-boot-starter-parent`). No `build.gradle`. Wrapper scripts `mvnw`/`mvnw.cmd` and `.mvn/` are present.
- REST is served by OfficeFloor via `officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter` (Spring Boot 4.x). DTOs generated by `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` 7.23.0; entity mapping by MapStruct.
- Test dependencies: `spring-boot-starter-test`, `spring-boot-starter-webmvc-test`, `spring-boot-starter-security-test`, `mockito-core`, `woof_test` (OfficeFloor test support), `json-path`, Jackson.
- Run the app: `./mvnw spring-boot:run` (readme.md).
- Run tests: `./mvnw test` (unit/acceptance via Surefire). Full build with tests: `./mvnw clean install` / `mvn clean install` (readme.md line 218). The acceptance tests run in-process against MockMvc, so no external server is needed.

One thing to flag for your task: the POST pipeline currently produces `registrationDate` (via `ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate`) as the only date field, and there is no `bulkSignupWarning` output in the pipeline or `Owner` schema even though `AcceptanceTest` asserts it — so that field is not yet implemented on the create path.

